nodecode-remesher is a rewrite of remesher's remesher/remesher:

  https://github.com/remesher/remesher
  commit 5f48a067722e10f0c08d368698fc03b05855bb89
  Apache-2.0, the repository's LICENSE unchanged (the plugin manifest names its
  author as Remesher)
  The plugin folder rewritten is integrations/hermes.

Rewritten: the plugin's four model-facing tools — remesher_health,
remesher_generate, remesher_job and remesher_assets — with their arguments
and answer shapes; the job receipt that outlives one call (queued, running,
succeeded, failed, timed_out, interrupted), kept as one JSON state file per
job under the profile's home; the one-active-job rule; the per-call deadline
of 1 to 1800 seconds, enforced by the bounded runner that kills the whole
process group; the artifact manifest with its SHA-256 and the GLB
header-and-length check, re-read and rehashed so a receipt whose files are
gone, changed or unreadable answers integrity_error instead of an artifact;
the environment scrub that keeps activation scripts, provider keys and
ambient CUDA/HF/Torch variables out of the child; and the three backends —
comfy3d passed through the CLI's config and workflow, native against a
numeric-loopback server, native-local with the CLI's own python and checkout
— with the loopback-origin check on the server setting. The Python
(subprocess, threading, hashlib) is Common Lisp here: nlk:run-bounded starts
the CLI, one section declaration for the settings, four nlk:define-contract
declarations for the tools' arguments, and nlk:sha256-text for the manifest.

Left out: the detached supervisor. The plugin forks a second interpreter per
job that survives the harness, consumes only queued receipts and holds the
deadline itself; here the job runs on a thread of the same image, so a
Nodecode that exits mid-job leaves a receipt saying running which a later
read reports as it stands, and the remote ComfyUI run is not cancelled by the
local deadline either way — the same caveat the original states. Also left
out, for scope rather than trouble: the native preset resolved into explicit
flags here becomes the CLI's own --native-preset, the per-call arguments the
original offers for native shape, atlas, camera angle and mesh repair
(remesher_generate keeps image, timeout_seconds, target_face_num and
native_preset), the REMESHER_SETTINGS file and REMESHER_* environment
settings (the config section is the one authority), the per-job native setup
snapshot, and the setup skill's walk through the CLI's native-setup
plan/check/apply — the README documents that step instead.
